Assembler Version 18
====================
Assembled by: version 17 (both instgen and asm)

Features Supported by This Assembler
-------------------------------------
All features from version 17, plus forward reference tracking and error
module extraction:

Syntax:
- Standard 6502 mnemonic syntax (LDA, STA, etc.)
- All addressing modes (immediate, zero page, absolute, indexed, indirect)
- DATA pseudo-instruction for raw byte emission
- Hex constants: $xx (1 byte) or $xxxx (2 bytes)
- Character literals in immediate mode (#'x') with escape sequences (\n, \\, \')
- Quoted strings in DATA with \n escape
- Label definitions with PC value or explicit assignment (label = value)
- Local labels with . prefix (.label), scoped to most recent global label
- PC setting via: * = $xxxx (with zero-fill on pass 2)
- Low byte (<) and high byte (>) operators on labels/values
- Comments with semicolons
- Two-pass assembly
- Automatic zero page vs absolute addressing based on value

Directives:
- .include filename - includes contents of another file
- .zeropage - switch to zero page section
- .code - switch to code section
- .data - declare raw byte data (same as DATA pseudo-instruction)

Error handling:
- Separate errors.asm module (extracted from main source)
- Error codes $01-$15 with descriptive messages
- Error messages include filename and line number
- File/line tracking via file stack
- Include traceback on errors (shows inclusion chain)

New in this version (relative to version 17):
- Forward reference tracking with FWDREF_LIST ($0200-$03FF)
  - IS_FWDREF flag for tracking unresolved labels in pass 1
  - Forward references force absolute addressing mode
  - fwdref.asm module: init, add, finalize, reset, check operations
  - Forward ref list verified between passes (debug mode)
- Error handling extracted into separate errors.asm module
  - to_decimal.asm included by errors.asm for decimal number display
- OPERAND_L/OPERAND_H variables for parsed operand values
- Addressing mode stored in ADDR_MODE variable
- INST_PTR_L/INST_PTR_H for instruction table entry pointer
- handle_fwdref_mode function for forward ref addressing mode resolution
- New errors: err_too_many_forward_refs ($13), err_invalid_operand ($14),
  err_unexpected_text ($15)

Features Used in This Assembler's Source Code
----------------------------------------------
- Standard 6502 mnemonic syntax (LDA, STA, JSR, etc.)
- All addressing modes including indirect indexed
- DATA pseudo-instruction for byte/string data
- Hex constants ($xx and $xxxx)
- Character literals in DATA ('\\', '\n', etc.)
- Quoted strings with escape sequences
- Labels and label assignments (e.g., MODE_NONE = $00)
- Local labels with . prefix
- PC setting (* = $2000 and * = $FFFC for vectors)
- Low byte (<) and high byte (>) operators
- Comments (;)
- BRK with inline error code and message string
- .include directive (environment.asm, common.asm, file_stack.asm,
  errors.asm, fwdref.asm, to_decimal.asm, out/inst.asm.out)
- .zeropage and .code directives
- Zero page variables via DATA $00

New syntax used in source (relative to version 17):
- None

Other source changes:
- Forward reference list at $0200 (FWDREF_LIST, FWDREF_LIMIT constants)
- IS_FWDREF zero page variable for forward reference tracking
- OPERAND_L, OPERAND_H zero page variables (separate from HEX1/HEX2)
- ADDR_MODE, INST_PTR_L, INST_PTR_H zero page variables
- Separate fwdref.asm module included
- Separate errors.asm module (error handlers extracted from main source)
- to_decimal.asm included by errors.asm (moved from direct include)
